1
00:00:02,630 --> 00:00:05,010
Hello everyone and welcome back to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:05,750
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:12,280
Katherine – My name is Katherine and today we have an intermediate level lesson for you English learners out there.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,280
Marco – That's right.

5
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,490
On this occasion, we are going on a diet.

6
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,070
So we're trying to lose weight.

7
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,400
Katherine – Uh-oh.

8
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:19,950
Well, there's a reason behind it.

9
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:23,030
Let's take a look at that reason in today's vocabulary preview.

10
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:25,960
Vocabulary Preview.

11
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:27,600
Marco – All right.

12
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:32,160
So today on Vocabulary Preview, we have a noun and it's a bridesmaid.

13
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:34,440
Katherine – A bridesmaid, a person.

14
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:37,720
So this is kind of like a job but it's a short job.

15
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,940
You do it when your friend gets married.

16
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:45,380
It's the person, the woman who stands next to her friend on the friend's wedding day.

17
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:46,640
Marco – That's right.

18
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:51,600
And usually bridesmaids want to lose weight because they have to get into this dress, right?

19
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,600
Katherine – That's right.

20
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,130
They have special dresses.

21
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,400
They have to make their friend look good.

22
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:00,320
They have to match each other actually because usually there's three or four girls.

23
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,440
They all have to wear the same outfit.

24
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:02,440
So it's very stressful.

25
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:03,440
Marco – Okay.

26
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:03,690
All right.

27
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:06,530
So we're going to see what's going on in this dialogue and we'll be back shortly.

28
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:18,400
Oh man, I've been starving myself for days now and I haven't lost an ounce.

29
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:19,840
Are you trying to lose weight?

30
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:23,860
Yeah, my friend is getting married next month and I'm supposed to be a bridesmaid.

31
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:28,080
I have to fit into my dress and look nice for her wedding, but I haven't lost any weight.

32
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:29,780
Look at these love handles.

33
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:32,780
You don't have to starve yourself to lose weight.

34
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,640
I think that's where you're going wrong.

35
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:35,440
Why?

36
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:39,200
If I eat less, then my body will start eating away at my fat reserves, right?

37
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:40,580
Not really.

38
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,260
You should try to not eat foods high in calories, salts or saturated fats.

39
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,180
Stay away from oily food and artificial flavors.

40
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:51,580
So you're saying that I should eat, but I should just watch what I eat?

41
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,220
Yes.

42
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:58,140
You should also try to reduce your intake of carbohydrates and foods that are high in cholesterol.

43
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:03,220
You can have steamed veggies or increase your protein intake found in chicken or fish.

44
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:07,240
If I do all of this, you think I can lose 20 pounds in four weeks?

45
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:09,000
Don't count on it.

46
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:12,000
All right.

47
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:13,340
We're back.

48
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:18,260
So I think there were a lot of interesting words related to food and to losing weight.

49
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:21,520
So why don't we take a look now at language takeaway.

50
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:24,960
Language takeaway.

51
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:31,700
Okay, this first phrase in language takeaway is a phrase that the girl says about herself.

52
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:32,900
She's trying to lose weight.

53
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:37,380
She's been starving herself or she says, I've been starving myself.

54
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,680
All right.

55
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,700
I've been starving myself.

56
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:44,880
So to starve yourself is to make yourself not eat.

57
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,800
That's right.

58
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:47,560
So to starve is a verb.

59
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,880
It means to not give someone food.

60
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:54,600
But to starve yourself, to starve oneself is reflexive.

61
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:57,760
I'm doing it to myself and it means that I'm not giving myself any food.

62
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:58,320
Okay.

63
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,400
So you're starving yourself basically to lose weight.

64
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:07,140
And she said, well, I've been starving myself for days and I haven't lost an ounce.

65
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:08,200
What is an ounce?

66
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:09,020
It's a good question.

67
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:11,280
An ounce is a kind of weight.

68
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:17,740
So like a kilogram or a gram or a pound, but an ounce is a very, very small measurement.

69
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Okay.

70
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,680
And this is in the imperial system.

71
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:28,240
So maybe a lot of our listeners aren't familiar with it, but usually for example, pounds and ounces go together just like grams and kilograms.

72
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:29,020
Exactly.

73
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:30,760
So I might be wrong.

74
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:33,160
I think there are 16 ounces in a pound.

75
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:36,680
So if you think about it, a pound, you say, oh, I lost a pound.

76
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:37,420
16 ounces.

77
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,700
She hasn't even lost an ounce.

78
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:41,720
It's a way to say she hasn't lost any weight yet.

79
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,720
All right.

80
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:47,380
So she was complaining about not losing weight and she said, look at these love handles.

81
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,600
What are love handles?

82
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:51,590
I love this phrase because you can like imagine them.

83
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:56,570
So imagine hugging someone and your hands are on their waist and maybe they have a little extra fat.

84
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,360
Those are like love handles.

85
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,890
You know, a handle is what you have on a door.

86
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,770
You turn the handle and the door opens.

87
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,200
But these are, this is fat on someone's side.

88
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:09,110
So a man or a woman can have fat on their hips and this is called love handles.

89
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:10,600
Okay.

90
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:10,750
So love handles.

91
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:15,030
It's a nice way of saying that extra little fat that people have on their sides.

92
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,040
All right.

93
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:24,950
And now talking more specifically about words related to food, we have one that maybe most of you are familiar with, calories.

94
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,480
Calories.

95
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:30,120
So calorie is a measurement of energy in food.

96
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:35,280
And so a lot of women and some men too like to avoid eating many calories.

97
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:39,360
They say, oh, that Snickers bar that has 1000 calories.

98
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:39,520
That's right.

99
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:47,320
If actually, if you look at your food labels, it usually says that you should have a daily diet should include more or less 2000 calories.

100
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,320
Exactly.

101
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:48,500
All right.

102
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,480
Another thing to avoid are saturated fats.

103
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:52,040
Okay.

104
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:54,660
So there's fat and there's saturated fat.

105
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:55,760
Marco, what's the difference?

106
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:56,840
I have no idea.

107
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:58,010
Come on.

108
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:01,330
There are two different types of fats.

109
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:02,600
Some of them are good for you.

110
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:04,800
Your body needs fat, right?

111
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:11,900
But saturated fats are the ones that are more difficult for your body to absorb and to make them work for you.

112
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:17,230
So usually they accumulate and that's why maybe they will, for example, make you a little bit fatter.

113
00:05:17,730 --> 00:05:19,670
So a lot of sweets have saturated fats.

114
00:05:20,010 --> 00:05:23,370
Oily foods have saturated fats and it's good to avoid those.

115
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,120
Right.

116
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:29,840
So stay away from saturated fats and artificial flavors.

117
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:32,410
So the word artificial can be used with many different things.

118
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,160
It means fake, not natural.

119
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:39,370
So you could say you have artificial flowers or artificial scents.

120
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:42,400
But in this case, we have artificial flavors.

121
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:45,000
That means fake flavors.

122
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,820
It's orange flavored, but there's no oranges.

123
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:48,890
It never came from an orange.

124
00:05:49,410 --> 00:05:55,130
You have to be careful with these because they use, because in many food products, chemicals are used.

125
00:05:55,130 --> 00:05:55,530
Right.

126
00:05:55,530 --> 00:05:56,670
And sugars, for example.

127
00:05:57,760 --> 00:06:05,040
So as you said, if you want to make something taste like orange, maybe they will use different chemicals and sugars to make it taste like orange.

128
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:05,230
Exactly.

129
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,950
The last thing we have to avoid is this word cholesterol.

130
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,200
Cholesterol.

131
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,200
Okay.

132
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:16,160
So these are found, for example, in eggs have a lot of cholesterol.

133
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:19,460
Or even just meats in general, like red meat.

134
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:27,600
And so people with heart problems are told to avoid cholesterol because it can actually, it can prevent the blood going to your heart.

135
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,880
It blocks up your heart.

136
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,620
So cholesterol is another bad one.

137
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:31,080
All right.

138
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:35,480
So all of these words are nouns and they're related to dieting and to food.

139
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:39,440
So I think we should listen to this dialogue again and keep a lookout for these words.

140
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:49,120
Oh man, I've been starving myself for days now and I haven't lost an ounce.

141
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,060
Are you trying to lose weight?

142
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:54,100
Yeah, my friend is getting married next month and I'm supposed to be a bridesmaid.

143
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:58,320
I have to fit into my dress and look nice for her wedding, but I haven't lost any weight.

144
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,020
Look at these love handles.

145
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:03,020
You don't have to starve yourself to lose weight.

146
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,880
I think that's where you're going wrong.

147
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:05,720
Why?

148
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:09,460
If I eat less than my body will start eating away at my fat reserves, right?

149
00:07:10,170 --> 00:07:10,750
Not really.

150
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:16,400
You should try to not eat foods high in calories, salts or saturated fats.

151
00:07:16,400 --> 00:07:18,450
Stay away from oily food and artificial flavors.

152
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:21,810
So you're saying that I should eat, but I should just watch what I eat?

153
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,600
Yes.

154
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:28,390
You can also try to reduce your intake of carbohydrates and foods that are high in cholesterol.

155
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:33,450
You can have steamed veggies or increase your protein intake found in chicken or fish.

156
00:07:33,970 --> 00:07:37,470
If I do all of this, you think I can lose 20 pounds in four weeks?

157
00:07:38,070 --> 00:07:39,230
Don't count on it.

158
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:44,680
All right, we're back.

159
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:47,170
We're going to take a look at two phrases on Fluency Builder.

160
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:49,590
Fluency Builder.

161
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:55,540
Okay, this first phrase is something that the girl who is dieting says.

162
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:58,600
She says, are you saying that I should eat?

163
00:07:58,980 --> 00:07:59,940
Because she's starving herself.

164
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,400
But that the important thing is that I watch what I eat.

165
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:05,020
So what is this watch what I eat?

166
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:05,400
All right.

167
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:10,660
So to watch what you eat is to be careful of what you eat or to take care.

168
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:13,960
So it doesn't actually mean to look at your food a lot.

169
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:15,400
You don't have to stare at your food.

170
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:19,220
You just have to be careful or to pay attention to what you're eating.

171
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,960
So you should watch what you eat.

172
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:22,840
So that means pay attention.

173
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,240
Does it have lots of calories?

174
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:25,920
Is there a lot of cholesterol?

175
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:27,020
Things like this.

176
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:27,360
Right.

177
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:32,360
For example, you may see signs in some places that say, watch your step.

178
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:33,860
So be careful where you're stepping.

179
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:35,100
Okay.

180
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:38,420
Well, this next phrase is the very last phrase.

181
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:41,240
The friend says, do you think I can lose 20 pounds?

182
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:45,000
And for those of you who use kilos, this is about eight kilos.

183
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:45,800
That's a lot of weight.

184
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:48,640
And the answer is don't count on it.

185
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:50,260
So what is this don't count on it?

186
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:50,720
All right.

187
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:51,720
Don't count on it.

188
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:53,000
Take that as a phrase.

189
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,880
It basically means that probably won't happen.

190
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:59,600
So you think you can come to my birthday party?

191
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:01,180
No, don't count on it.

192
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:01,720
I'll be busy.

193
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:05,440
Oh, so that means that means he probably won't.

194
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,500
Marco probably won't come.

195
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:07,760
Right.

196
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:11,800
So you shouldn't expect it to happen because he can't promise that it will.

197
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,040
Yeah.

198
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:13,200
That's a good way of putting it.

199
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:14,660
Don't expect it to happen.

200
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:18,700
So for example, don't count on winning the lottery anytime soon.

201
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:19,240
Why not?

202
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,920
Because it's very difficult, right?

203
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:22,940
So don't count on it.

204
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:26,230
Or you can say, don't count on this train being on time.

205
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:27,910
It's always at least a half an hour late.

206
00:09:28,130 --> 00:09:28,430
Exactly.

207
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,440
All right.

208
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:30,890
So many different examples there.

209
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,630
I think we should listen to a dialogue for the last time.

210
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:46,260
Oh man, I've been starving myself for days now and I haven't lost an ounce.

211
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:47,840
Are you trying to lose weight?

212
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:51,880
Yeah, my friend is getting married next month and I'm supposed to be a bridesmaid.

213
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:56,100
I have to fit into my dress and look nice for her wedding, but I haven't lost any weight.

214
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:57,760
Look at these love handles.

215
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,800
You don't have to starve yourself to lose weight.

216
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:02,660
I think that's where you're going wrong.

217
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:03,440
Why?

218
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:07,220
If I eat less, then my body will start eating away at my fat reserves, right?

219
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:08,560
Not really.

220
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:13,280
You should try to not eat foods high in calories, salts, or saturated fats.

221
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:16,200
Stay away from oily food and artificial flavors.

222
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:19,580
So you're saying that I should eat, but I should just watch what I eat?

223
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:20,220
Yes.

224
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:26,000
You can also try to reduce your intake of carbohydrates and foods that are high in cholesterol.

225
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:31,220
You can have steamed veggies or increase your protein intake found in chicken or fish.

226
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:35,240
If I do all of this, you think I can lose 20 pounds in four weeks?

227
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:37,000
Don't count on it.

228
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:42,920
Alright, we're back.

229
00:10:42,950 --> 00:10:44,630
So these are some pretty healthy tips, right?

230
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,960
Watch what you eat and don't starve yourself.

231
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:47,270
Absolutely.

232
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:51,610
Starving yourself, I think is, well, obviously very unhealthy.

233
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:55,030
To starve, to die of starvation, that's the noun.

234
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,920
Not a very pretty way to go.

235
00:10:57,970 --> 00:11:02,070
I've actually also heard that people that start to eat less, right?

236
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:14,340
To maybe just eat once a day, their body actually thinks that there isn't much food around, so they start to store up these fats and these calories, energy, instead of releasing them normally.

237
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:20,100
So instead of actually losing weight, you actually gain weight because the moment that you eat, your body stores everything.

238
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:20,960
Exactly.

239
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:30,620
So instead of getting rid of those good fats, your body stores them with the saturated fats and you are doing the opposite to your body that you should be doing.

240
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:44,740
So the best recommendation that I've always heard is to avoid eating too much red meat, balance your diet out, eat lots of fruit as well, have those good sugars, and avoid artificial foods.

241
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:46,640
Drink a lot of water.

242
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:47,500
Drink a lot of water and exercise.

243
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:48,420
Exercise, yeah.

244
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:49,500
This is the key thing.

245
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:56,600
I think many people rely only on dieting or eating less, but actually nothing can take its place more than exercise.

246
00:11:56,600 --> 00:12:06,000
And exercise is really great because it tones those muscles, so once you actually lose the weight, you feel good, you have muscles, you have more energy, and it helps you sleep.

247
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Right.

248
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,000
